graph TB
    A[Server Architectures] --> B[Iterative Server]
    A --> C[Concurrent Forking]
    A --> D[Pre-forked Workers]
    A --> E[Threaded Server]
    A --> F[Thread Pool]
    A --> G[Event-Driven epoll]
    
    B --> B1[accept → process → accept]
    B --> B2[One client at a time]
    B --> B3[Simple but blocks]
    
    C --> C1[accept → fork → child handles]
    C --> C2[Parallel clients]
    C --> C3[High overhead]
    
    D --> D1[Pre-fork N workers]
    D --> D2[Workers share accept]
    D --> D3[Lower fork cost]
    
    E --> E1[accept → pthread_create]
    E --> E2[Lighter than processes]
    E --> E3[Shared memory issues]
    
    F --> F1[Pre-create thread pool]
    F --> F2[Queue work items]
    F --> F3[No thread creation overhead]
    
    G --> G1[Single-threaded event loop]
    G --> G2[epoll monitors all clients]
    G --> G3[Non-blocking I/O]
    G --> G4[Scales to 10k+ connections]
    
